#: src/languages/ruby.md:19
msgid "Language Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:21
msgid ""
"There are multiple language servers available for Ruby. Zed supports the two "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:26
msgid ""
"They both have an overlapping feature set of autocomplete, diagnostics, code "
"actions, etc. and it's up to you to decide which one you want to use. Note "
"that you can't use both at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:28
msgid "In addition to these two language servers, Zed also supports:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:30
msgid ""
"[rubocop](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop) which is a static code "
"analyzer and linter for Ruby. Under the hood, it's also used by Zed as a "
"language server, but its functionality is complimentary to that of "
"solargraph and ruby-lsp."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:31
msgid ""
"[sorbet](https://sorbet.org/) which is a static type checker for Ruby with a "
"custom gradual type system."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:32
msgid ""
"[steep](https://github.com/soutaro/steep) which is a static type checker for "
"Ruby that uses Ruby Signature (RBS)."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:33
msgid ""
"[Herb](https://herb-tools.dev) which is a language server for ERB files."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/ruby.md:35
msgid ""
"When configuring a language server, it helps to open the LSP Logs window "
"using the 'dev: Open Language Server Logs' command. You can then choose the "
"corresponding language instance to see any logged information."
msgstr ""

